  <!-- ============ 7 SYNC ============ -->
  <section>
    <h2>Cluster eight <em>&#183; 12 tables</em></h2>
    <h3>Directory sync</h3>
    <p class="lede">The largest cluster. Pulling staff out of a hotel's directory is not a nightly script &mdash; it is a resumable, leased, fenced, paged, auditable job, and every one of those words is a table.</p>

    <div class="frame">
<div class="zoomable">
<pre class="mermaid">
erDiagram
  ProvisioningConnections {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier FederatedAuthorityId FK
    bit IsEnabled
    nvarchar Schedule
  }
  ApprovedProvisioningGroups {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    nvarchar DirectoryGroupId "the allowlist"
    nvarchar MapsToRoleCode
  }
  DirectoryGroupMemberships {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    nvarchar MemberSubject
  }
  DirectorySyncRuns {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    bigint RunNumber
    int Outcome
  }
  DirectorySyncRunItems {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier RunId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    uniqueidentifier SupersededByItemId FK
    int Action "created changed held"
  }
  DirectorySyncRunStreams {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier RunId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    uniqueidentifier ApprovedProvisioningGroupId FK
    uniqueidentifier DirectorySyncStreamStateId FK
  }
  DirectorySyncRunPages {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier RunId FK
    uniqueidentifier RunStreamId FK
    int PageNumber
  }
  DirectorySyncStreamStates {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    uniqueidentifier ApprovedProvisioningGroupId FK
    nvarchar DeltaToken "resume point"
  }
  DirectorySyncRunSequence {
    uniqueidentifier TenantId PK
    bigint Next
  }
  ProvisioningLeases {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    datetimeoffset ExpiresAtUtc
  }
  ProvisioningFencingSequence {
    uniqueidentifier TenantId PK
    uniqueidentifier ConnectionId FK
    bigint Token
  }
  MigrationAmbiguities {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId FK
    uniqueidentifier UserAccountId FK
    int State "waiting on a human"
  }
  FederatedAuthorities {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
  }
  UserAccounts {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
  }

  FederatedAuthorities ||--o{ ProvisioningConnections : "synced from"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ ApprovedProvisioningGroups : "allows only"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ DirectoryGroupMemberships : "read back"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ DirectorySyncRuns : "ran"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunItems : "touched"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunStreams : "streamed"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ DirectorySyncStreamStates : "cursor for"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ ProvisioningLeases : "locked by"
  ProvisioningConnections ||--o{ ProvisioningFencingSequence : "fenced by"
  DirectorySyncRuns ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunItems : "processed"
  DirectorySyncRuns ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunStreams : "opened"
  DirectorySyncRuns ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunPages : "fetched"
  DirectorySyncRunStreams ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunPages : "page of"
  DirectorySyncRunItems |o--o{ DirectorySyncRunItems : "superseded by"
  ApprovedProvisioningGroups ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunStreams : "for group"
  ApprovedProvisioningGroups ||--o{ DirectorySyncStreamStates : "for group"
  DirectorySyncStreamStates ||--o{ DirectorySyncRunStreams : "resumed from"
  DirectorySyncRunSequence ||--o{ DirectorySyncRuns : "numbers"
  UserAccounts ||--o{ MigrationAmbiguities : "could not match"
</pre>
</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ 8 PLUMBING ============ -->
  <section>
    <h2>Cluster nine <em>&#183; 3 tables</em></h2>
    <h3>Plumbing</h3>
    <p class="lede">Present identically in both databases today, which is why the merge nets fifty rather than fifty-three.</p>

    <div class="frame">
<div class="zoomable">
<pre class="mermaid">
erDiagram
  OutboxMessages {
    uniqueidentifier Id PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId
    nvarchar Type
    nvarchar Status
    datetimeoffset PublishedAtUtc
  }
  InboxMessages {
    nvarchar MessageId PK
    nvarchar Consumer PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId
    datetimeoffset ProcessedAtUtc
  }
  RequestIdempotency {
    nvarchar Key PK
    uniqueidentifier TenantId
    nvarchar ResponseHash
  }
</pre>
</div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px"><code>OutboxMessages</code> is what makes the whole estate work without synchronous calls: events are written in the same transaction as the data that caused them, then published. A tenant is never created without the event that tells the other forty-five services about it.</p>
  </section>

