  <!-- ============ RULES ============ -->
  <section>
    <h2>What a foreign key cannot say</h2>
    <h3>Three rules, each with its own constraint</h3>
    <pre class="sql"><b>one brand per hotel</b>
  UNIQUE (TenantId, PropertyId)
    WHERE ToUtc IS NULL AND TypeCode = 'Brand'

  the TypeCode copy on the member row is what makes this a single-table
  filtered index. Without it the rule needs a trigger, and a trigger is
  a rule you find out about at three in the morning.

<b>a role is scoped to a hotel or a group, never both</b>
  CHECK ((PropertyId IS NULL) &lt;&gt; (PropertyGroupId IS NULL))

<b>BrandDetails may only extend a Brand group</b>
  TypeCode column, CHECK (TypeCode = 'Brand'), and a composite FK
  against UNIQUE (TenantId, Id, TypeCode) on PropertyGroups

  attach brand detail to a Region group and the insert fails,
  not the code review</pre>

    <div class="callout">
      <h4>Where to start</h4>
      <p><strong>Organisation and Currencies first</strong> &mdash; money and law before anything else, because retrofitting a tax regime after real folios exist means migrating money. Then <code>UserAccounts</code> (ten tables reference it), <code>FederatedAuthorities</code> (every login path starts there), and <code>ProvisioningConnections</code> (seven tables, and the hardest to retrofit).</p>
      <p>The migration traps, in order of how quietly they fail: <code>NameAr</code> on the group, <code>ThemeReference</code> on the details, <code>IsActive</code>. Each is a working feature that disappears without an error.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    Updated 22 September 2026. Existing tables and columns read from the live <span style="font-family:var(--mono)">remy_identity</span> and <span style="font-family:var(--mono)">remy_platform</span> databases and from <span style="font-family:var(--mono)">Remy.Platform.Domain</span>; new fields are justified in the gap analysis and placed by the boundary analysis. Attribute lists are trimmed to keys and the columns that carry meaning &mdash; audit columns and the <span style="font-family:var(--mono)">Version</span> rowversion are on every table and are not repeated.
  </footer>

</div>

<script>
  (function () {
    var STEPS = [0.5, 0.65, 0.8, 1, 1.25, 1.6, 2, 2.6, 3.4, 4.4, 5.6, 7, 8.5, 10];
    var BASE = 3;

    function controls(target, frame) {
      var i = BASE;
      var bar = document.createElement('div');
      bar.className = 'zoombar';

      function btn(label, aria) {
        var b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button';
        b.textContent = label;
        if (aria) b.setAttribute('aria-label', aria);
        return b;
      }
      var out = document.createElement('select');
      out.className = 'zlevel';
      out.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Zoom level');
      for (var z = 0; z < STEPS.length; z++) {
        var o = document.createElement('option');
        o.value = String(z);
        o.textContent = Math.round(STEPS[z] * 100) + '%';
        out.appendChild(o);
      }
      out.addEventListener('change', function () { i = +out.value; apply(); });
      var minus = btn('\u2212', 'Zoom out');
      var plus = btn('+', 'Zoom in');
      var reset = btn('Reset');
      var hint = document.createElement('span');
      hint.className = 'hint';
      hint.textContent = 'up to 1000% · scroll inside the frame to pan';

      var natural = 0;

      function apply() {
        var k = STEPS[i];
        out.value = String(i);
        minus.disabled = i === 0;
        plus.disabled = i === STEPS.length - 1;

        // Mermaid renders the svg at width:100% of its box, so scaling the box is a
        // no-op: the svg simply re-fits. Size the svg itself instead. The viewBox
        // does the rest, so it stays vector-sharp at any level.
        var svg = target.querySelector('svg');
        if (svg) {
          if (!natural) natural = svg.getBoundingClientRect().width || svg.clientWidth;
          if (natural) {
            svg.style.maxWidth = 'none';
            svg.style.width = Math.round(natural * k) + 'px';
            svg.style.height = 'auto';
          }
        }

        // above 100% the diagram would push the page open, so cap the frame and let it scroll
        if (k > 1 && !frame.classList.contains('tall')) {
          frame.style.maxHeight = '78vh';
          frame.style.overflow = 'auto';
        } else if (!frame.classList.contains('tall')) {
          frame.style.maxHeight = '';
          frame.style.overflow = '';
        }
      }

      // mermaid renders after this script runs, so measure once it has
      if (window.requestAnimationFrame) {
        var tries = 0;
        (function settle() {
          if (target.querySelector('svg') || tries++ > 120) { apply(); return; }
          requestAnimationFrame(settle);
        })();
      }
      minus.addEventListener('click', function () { if (i > 0) { i--; apply(); } });
      plus.addEventListener('click', function () { if (i < STEPS.length - 1) { i++; apply(); } });
      reset.addEventListener('click', function () { i = BASE; apply(); frame.scrollLeft = 0; frame.scrollTop = 0; });

      bar.appendChild(minus);
      bar.appendChild(out);
      bar.appendChild(plus);
      bar.appendChild(reset);
      bar.appendChild(hint);
      frame.parentNode.insertBefore(bar, frame);
      apply();
    }

    var zoomables = document.querySelectorAll('.zoomable');
    for (var k = 0; k < zoomables.length; k++) {
      var z = zoomables[k];
      var frame = z.closest ? z.closest('.frame') : z.parentNode;
      if (frame) controls(z, frame);
    }
  })();
</script>
